      },
      "analysis": "Skill memory is empty (generation 0). Across 20 native trajectories the agent already locates users by name+zip when email is unknown, matches referenced items by reading all order details, applies status-based eligibility (pending cancel/modify vs delivered return/exchange), and computes exact totals with the calculate tool. The failures are not random: 5 finished with reward 0, mostly via max_steps, and they share one recurring dysfunction — the customer's strategy of chaining alternatives and asking repeated policy/hypothetical/fee questions before finalizing causes the agent to re-confirm the same plan many times, enumerate options over and over, and often execute the once-per-order tool call only at the very last step with no turn left to deliver the closing confirmation (tasks 8, 67, 106, 80; task 22 also expired in Q&A). A second, smaller evidence point is a real tool error when an exchange grouped items that actually lived in two different orders (task 107), which the agent fixed by splitting per-order calls. This supports one reusable procedural repair: drive order-action requests to completion — verify item-to-order membership, confirm once with exact amounts, execute promptly per order, and answer hypothetical policy questions concisely without re-opening the full plan. This is a capability gap (no skill exists) and the guidance stays subordinate to the stated policy (explicit confirmation, once-per-order modify/exchange, status checks).",
