            "guidance": "Locate the authenticated user’s orders by retrieving details for all of their orders and match the referenced items by product/attributes before choosing a tool. Verify order status first (pending = cancel/modify; delivered = return/exchange) and ensure all items to be changed for a single order are collected into one list before the once-per-order modify/exchange call; if the referenced items are in different orders, prepare a separate call per order. Present the concrete plan once, including per-item changes and exact net amounts (sum amounts with the calculate tool), and ask for one explicit confirmation. When the user asks 'why' or policy questions, answer them briefly by citing the applicable policy/backend constraint, then return to the single pending confirmation instead of re-listing all options or re-asking the same confirmation. If the user adds items or changes scope after the plan was agreed, fold the additions into the pending single per-order call rather than starting over, and re-confirm only the changed scope. On an explicit 'yes', execute the confirmed tool call(s) promptly — one call at a time per order — and then immediately send the closing summary (new status, exact amounts, refund method/timing, and that instructions will be emailed) without seeking further confirmation."
